# v2's menger as the service under test (V2-44): tests/conformance.rs runs
#   python3 -I conformance/run.py run --role service --url ws://127.0.0.1:PORT --key KEYFILE --max-calls 8 --idle-secs 3 \
#       --max-per-principal 8 --origin-allowed http://127.0.0.1:SHELL_PORT --expect-fail menger/tests/conformance-v2.expect
# (menger started with --max-calls-per-connection 8 --idle-timeout-secs 3 --max-connections-per-principal 8
# --max-connections-per-agent 8: the kit's key is a `key:` principal, an agent since V2-31).
# plexus-wire's conformance/expect/menger.txt is main's; this is v2's — main's lines but schema.child_via_call
# (v2 has no chats, so it passes), and paging.walk (PERF-15's rows pages) and limits.quota (V2-31's split), v2's own.
# One line per test: <test id>  <gap ticket>  <why>. A line whose test passes fails the run as "fixed — remove the entry".
call.malformed            POLYGLOT-11  a {ns}.call with unreadable params answers -32603 Internal error; the spec says -32602
schema.unknown_method     POLYGLOT-11  {ns}.schema {method} naming no method answers -32603; the spec says -32602
paging.walk               V2-46        the kit reads a summary item per row; v2's tickets.list answers rows { items } pages (PERF-15)
limits.quota              V2-48        V2-31 counts a principal's connections at its first call (in band), not at the upgrade (429)
input.not_this_call       BIDIR-6      runs plexus 0.7 from crates.io, and the input half is not published (BIDIR-6)
input.credit_first        BIDIR-6      no method of this service declares `input`
input.in_order            BIDIR-6      no method of this service declares `input`
input.end_with_seq        BIDIR-6      no method of this service declares `input`
input.past_credit         BIDIR-6      no method of this service declares `input`
input.closed_before_done  BIDIR-6      no method of this service declares `input`
